  assign comp_search_blobs = 'book links short story writing competition writing a nice low-key one for upper primary writers. $100 prize plus the winning story published on the book links website. open theme. writing national|territory young scientists awards stem nt kids build a bug from pre-used materials and explain where it lives, or make a crocwise poster. top 3 in every category at every year level win cash. science,stem,art,writing nt|acmf national songwriting competition performance nearly $20,000 in prizes, all paid towards musical equipment or tuition. a breakthrough comp for any kid who writes songs in their bedroom. music national|tasmanian science talent search stem tasmanian kids from kinder to year 12 decode the universe with a picture book, photo essay, video or invention. kinder to year 2 gets its own division. science,stem,writing,art,photography tas|nunga kids art competition art flagship run by sa’s commissioner for aboriginal children and young people. first nations kids’ art on the children’s day theme is displayed during naidoc week. art,culture sa|poetry in action poetry competition writing one original poem, any australian school kid. winner takes $1,000 and their poem joins performances seen by over 100,000 students. poet keeps copyright. writing,poetry national|artstart at the queen victoria museum and art gallery art for 25 years, teachers across northern tasmania have sent in student art. selected pieces are hung, professionally presented, in a real museum gallery. art tas (northern tasmania)|save the frogs! art contest art international frog conservation through art. open to all ages and free to enter, so aussie kids are welcome. quirky, niche and surprisingly popular. art,environment international|national schools poster competition (nspc) social good kids design and run their own investigation, then share what they found on a digital poster. cash prizes per division, plus a sustainability stream. science,stem,environment national|flickerfest flickerup (australian national youth competition) photography & film the youth arm of flickerfest, australia’s academy award qualifying short film festival. winning films screen at bondi beside the international lineup. film national|children’s week national poster competition art civic the winning drawing becomes the real national children’s week poster, printed and sent to schools, libraries and councils around the country. art,culture national|international festival of owls kids’ art contest art international a small us festival comp that now draws entries from dozens of countries. a perfect home for kids who love owls. original art only, posted to minnesota. art international (postal to usa)|australian cartoonists association prize (in theinmag) art in the mag going since 1924. the aca picks a winner from the cartoons kids send in to theinmag each issue. the winner gets a year of inkspot, their own magazine. art national|camp australia big art comp art brand-led camp australia runs a national art comp every term. past prizes include hoodies printed with kids’ own art and a trophy designed by the brickman himself. art national|crayola creative acts of color (open call) art brand-led crayola’s year-round open call. less about winning, more about joining a global creative movement. kids share what they make, tagged #staycreative. art international|state premier’s reading challenges writing reading not a competition, a challenge. read books from your state’s list and earn a certificate signed by the premier. a big motivator for reluctant readers. reading nsw, qld, vic, wa, sa, tas|theinmag - publishing real creative kids everything in the mag your drawing, story or comic on a real printed page, in the hands of thousands of kids across australia. send in anything you’ve made, any time. send it in. art,writing,photography,music,comedy national|sydney royal easter show - junior arts & crafts art royal show australia’s biggest creativity showcase, running since